    "done_when": "First reproduce at base: a manifest with status complete, a commit, a tests line and an empty negative_control_log audits with no finding (the currency report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/s22-coord/scoring-currency/report.md shows the call). Then, when the run armed a negative control, audit_manifest refuses each shape in §2j's table of control shapes (read it in the plan) with a finding that names the field and what it found, and accepts a control log that resolves to a readable file ending in a bare EXIT= line with a non-zero code. A run that armed no control, and a manifest carrying a recorded waiver, raise no control finding. A new tests/test_a_control_log_is_judged_at_write.py asserts each refused shape, the accepted shape, the no-control case and the waiver case through audit_manifest and through the crew check-manifest console script. The named negative control (remove the new control-log check) reddens the empty-log case. The gate is that new test plus tests/test_manifest_check_command.py, tests/test_worker_prompt_contract.py and tests/test_a_review_manifest_passes_its_own_check.py, run at base and at head. Each arm is recorded as JSON carrying completed true and a literal command with absolute paths and no angle-bracket placeholder; each log names its revision on the first line and ends with a bare line reading EXIT= followed by the exit code. Every pytest process uses a basetemp private to that process. The head arm adds no failure id; any added id means status blocked, naming each id. ruff check and ruff format --check over the changed paths report no finding the base did not. Scratch goes under /tmp in a directory named for this run and is deleted before status complete, printed and listed in artifacts. An evidence fragment at docs/evidence/fragments/scoring-should-stop-a-promotion/a-control-log-is-judged-at-write.html records the change. The turn ends once the manifest reads complete or blocked.",
